<p>A fully loaded Kuwait-flagged oil tanker, the Al Salmi, caught fire after what Kuwait Petroleum Corporation and several news outlets described as an Iranian strike while the vessel was anchored near Dubai on Monday, with reports published Tuesday. The ship’s owner said the hull was damaged and at first warned of a possible spill, but Dubai authorities later said emergency teams had put out the fire, all crew were safe, and no oil had leaked into surrounding waters. The strike came amid broader escalation in the Gulf and around the Strait of Hormuz. On Monday, President Trump warned that the United States would target Iran’s energy infrastructure if Iran did not reopen the strait, while multiple reports said the tanker attack was the latest in a series of assaults on merchant shipping since U.S. and Israeli attacks on Iran on Feb. 28. One clear piece of good news in a tense story: officials contained the immediate maritime emergency without reported injuries or an oil spill, avoiding what could have become a much larger environmental incident.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/NdbXaKSTYJIQ7Jn_XJZcFkMI-9dREQLEdVtWCukrZRag-Cb1Juh0sVS9ngpWWcZ0cN3CTCs2uQWRTrEiXWCi2nYI7w6QvWCoOJE1Dz8IGr3dVKACm97FnXPleGRXQ8FTplt-JlCjY0DwEGsTC9XdBmo6Y2fJp0FxZ8J95OvltHIpXmznPo1D2Rd0SJQiUEHmCuOD94qFyIOrV_g' alt='The Dubai port in the United Arab Emirates in 2022.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Regional air defenses: Saudi Arabia and Kuwait both reported defensive activity during the same period of escalation.</li><li>Wider conflict zone: The Israeli military said four soldiers were killed in combat in southern Lebanon as clashes with Hezbollah continued during the same regional crisis.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Kuwait Petroleum Corporation: The state oil company identified Iran as responsible and said the Al Salmi was fully loaded at the time of the incident. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/kuwait-says-oil-tanker-hit-in-iranian-attack-at-dubai-port/article70805571.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Dubai authorities: Dubai officials said response teams contained the incident and later confirmed that no oil had leaked into surrounding waters. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/31/kuwaiti-tanker-hit-by-iranian-attack-in-dubai-port-raising-oil-spill-fears'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>President Trump: The president said the United States would obliterate Iran’s energy plants and oil wells if the Strait of Hormuz was not reopened. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/giant-oil-tanker-dubai-hit-iranian-strike-trump-threatens-obliterate-iran-energy'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/03/30/world/iran-war-trump-oil-news'>Kuwaiti Tanker Full of Oil Struck Off Dubai Day After Trump’s Threats</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/kuwait-says-oil-tanker-hit-in-iranian-attack-at-dubai-port/article70805571.ece'>Kuwait says oil tanker hit in Iranian attack at Dubai port;  crew safe</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/giant-oil-tanker-dubai-hit-iranian-strike-trump-threatens-obliterate-iran-energy'>Giant oil tanker off Dubai hit by Iranian strike, Trump threatens to obliterate Iran energy, oil plants</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/mar/31/iran-latest-updates-trump-threats-oil-spill-dubai-tehran-jerusalem-strikes'>Middle East crisis live: Iran attacks tanker in Dubai; explosions in Tehran and Jerusalem amid wave of strikes</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/fully-loaded-kuwaiti-oil-tanker-damaged-in-iranian-strike-near-dubai-middle-east-conflict-11289174#publisher=newsstand'>Fully Loaded Kuwaiti Oil Tanker Damaged In Iranian Strike Near Dubai</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/giant-oil-tanker-off-dubai-hit-by-iranian-strike-t